<mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.413em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-var\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2032\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D451 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"block\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mo data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">″</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><msup><mi>y</mi><mo data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>\nwe can use Euler's method to approximate a solution by first reducing the second-order ODE to a system of first-order ODEs,\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"227\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mrow><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-s4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7B TEX-S4\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 11.724em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"t