    "q-77008": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 38",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14212321/assets/dea7eed9213ddf1bb3293950e2490b120a061e9add1172d3b850ccbc58f90454.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4$ traversed from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,-1).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Notice that we can write its equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, our curve is a part-ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $2$ and $1$ respectively. This curve can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2(-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,dt \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-1+0]-[1-0] \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77008-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "0",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"843\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77008-b",
